  "note": "Independent re-audit against RFC 8050 Section 2 (\"MRT parsers are usually stateless.  In order to parse BGP messages that contain data structures that depend on the capabilities negotiated during the BGP session setup, the MRT subtypes are utilized.\"). Re-read all 21 tagged test entries across internal/mrt, internal/analyze, and internal/component/bgp/reactor, plus all cited producers including the updated OnBGPMessage and observedBGPWriter.observe -> selected_refresh_eor.go::complete. On the parser side, TestRFC8050NoOPENSubtypeDecodesExactNLRI proves stateless decoding without OPENs across both TypeBGP4MP and TypeBGP4MPET, all eight BGP4MP subtypes (1, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11 \u2014 both 2-byte and 4-byte AS, received and LOCAL), and all six isolated NLRI locations, asserting exact prefixes, exact Path Identifiers (0 and 0x01020304 vs empty), and unchanged message bytes; TestIsAddPathHelpers covers all five RIB and four BGP4MP ADD-PATH subtypes vs base subtypes; TestRFC8050SubtypeControlsEveryNLRILocation verifies all eight subtypes and rejects truncated Path Identifiers in all four NLRI locations; TestRFC8050SessionContextDecodesMixedDirections, TestMRTContextCapabilityASNBoundaries (including narrow 2-byte AS_TRANS matching OnBGPMessage's new !as4 capping), TestMRTEmptyMPFamilyRequiresContext, TestRFC8050CommandsReadSubtypeContext, and TestRFC8050CommandsRequireMixedContext prove directional OPEN context for mixed-family UPDATEs and explicit ErrContextUnavailable refusal across all six CLI commands when context is missing, stale, mismatched, or ambiguous. Live collision and migration tests (TestMRTWinningCollisionPreservesOPEN, TestMRTCollisionWinnerReservation, TestMRTMigrationEpochUsesActualLocalOPEN) and TestRFC8050MessageCallbackPreservesEncodingAndFraming confirm original OPEN and frame preservation through observeReceivedWire, observe -> complete (whose completeEOR is read-only), adoptIncoming, and OnBGPMessage. Verdict: enforced.",
